Subject: Cantor EVO-X2 Remote Preflight Private Permit Bridge P0 Justification

@ [justification_uuid] c284fca3-477a-42f1-92de-9e12a2734243
@ [canonical_uuid] 06d82d16-143a-4abb-9c70-c03163285842

& [WhyNow]
  + published pure activation can verify supplied correspondence and the published runner can execute only with an unconstructible permit
  + the exact missing seam is therefore capability transfer rather than another parser process adapter or authority source

& [WhyPrivate]
  + a public constructor bridge or CLI would silently convert repository eligibility into physical authority
  + crate-private visibility and absent production admission construction keep the bridge type-checked but unreachable

& [WhyOwnership]
  + Rust moves and FnOnce make one admission one permit and one runner entry easier to audit than mutable counters alone
  + a terminal non-capability result prevents uncertain failure from returning retry authority

& [WhyIndependentReceipt]
  + a successful function return is not sufficient evidence; canonical reparse and the existing validator must agree on the retained runner receipt

& [WhyFormationFirst]
  + even unreachable capability code changes the repository's future authority topology and must follow published source full SJS formation verification and bookend

& [Decision]
  + form sign verify publish and bookend the private bridge contract before any Rust issuer or bridge module is added
